Two exported aliases of one unexported target, both spelled in a single rendered type.
Nothing produces the map, so it becomes an injector input and its spelling lands in the
generated signature. Each alias is judged on its own exported name and the target is
never named, so this generates and compiles. The alias exemption from the visited-set
dedup must not over-reject, and visiting sibling aliases of one target must work even
though they are identical to each other under the visited set's keying.
-- config --
import-path: example.com/app
package-name: app
output: plumb_gen.go
-- example.com/lib/lib.go --
package lib

type hidden struct{ X int }
type A1 = hidden
type A2 = hidden
type Thing struct{}

//plumb:build
func New(m map[A1]A2) *Thing { return &Thing{} }
